    "knowledge_point": "Z-Score: Word Problems",
    "problem": "The mean weight of a group of ballet dancers is $45\\text{ kg}.$ One of the dancers in the ballet group weighs $38\\text{ kg}$, and her $z$-score is $-2.5.$ Find the standard deviation of the weight of the dancers in the ballet group.",
    "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=38,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=45,$ and $z=-2.5$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 38 & =45+(-2.5)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -7 & =-2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{-7}{-2.5} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the standard deviation of the ballet dancer's weights is $2.8\\,\\text{kg}.$",
