    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. No prior submitted answers or grades were supplied. q-60139: Each ratio unit represents 20/4=5 people, so there are 35 children and 55 people altogether. q-147075: There are 3×7=21 total digits, hence 21−7=14 odd digits. q-147076: There are 24×3/2=36 total cells, hence 12 green cells. q-147213: There are 14×7/2=49 total buttons, hence 35 green buttons. q-48965: The quotient rule gives [5(−2)(−5+6)−(5(−1)+4)(1)]/(−5+6)^2=−9. q-288596: A nonzero right-hand side makes the equation unsolvable precisely when q+9=0, so q=−9. q-288143: Similarly, −3(q+4)=0 gives q=−4. q-94460: z=(14−28)/sqrt(3.60)≈−7.38. q-94457: z=(10.5−6)/sqrt(10.8)≈1.37. q-17237: The mean is x−zσ=35.4−(−1.1)(10.5)=46.95. q-94471: σ=(20−14.5)/2.2=2.5. q-94519: σ=(38−45)/(−2.5)=2.8 kg. q-9785: Convert 350 g to 0.350 kg; z=(3−3.2)/0.350≈−0.57. The source uses an equality sign for this rounded value, but the requested two-decimal answer is correct. q-75924: For x≠0, clearing denominators gives 2x+6=4x, so x=3. q-75925: For x≠0, clearing denominators gives x−2=3+5x, so x=−5/4. q-14738: Clearing denominators requires p≠0 and yields 9=p+9, forcing the excluded value p=0; therefore there is no solution.",
